WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.126
Group equivariant convolutions taught networks to
share parameters across rotations and flips,

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:10.682
dramatically improving data efficiency for
geometric transformations.

00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:15.172
Yet photometric changes, such as shifts in hue, had
been left aside.

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:20.850
Studies of trained CNNs show that early layers
learn strongly color-selective neurons,

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.547
which suggests color is a natural axis for equivariance.

00:00:24.627 --> 00:00:30.688
This motivates treating a hue shift the same way
prior work treated a rotation: as a symmetry

00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:33.131
the network should respect by design,

00:00:33.211 --> 00:00:36.300
rather than something it must relearn from data.
